.TH CUBE-CHROOTABLES-STUDIO 1 "2026-10-31" "Cube Chrootables" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cube-chrootables-studio, cube-chrootables-manager \- Debian image workspace desktop and CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cube-chrootables-studio
.RI [ --store " directory" ]
.RB [ --demo ]
.RB [ --version ]
.br
.B cube-chrootables-manager
.RB [ --help ]
.RB [ --doctor ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create Debian workspaces, open embedded terminals, save recovery points,
clone, import and export images. Studio coexists with Whitecube's
cube-chrootables and the standalone chrootables-desktop.
.PP
Run the desktop as your normal user. Unlock store opens a terminal running
sudo; no graphical authentication agent is required. The administrator helper
ends when the store is locked or the window closes, after active work finishes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --store " directory"
Select an absolute workspace store other than the host root.
.TP
.B --demo
Explore sample data without changing a workspace store or saving preferences.
.TP
.B --version
Print the Cube application version. The CLI prints the upstream engine version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/chrootable-manager
Default shared image, snapshot, export and operation store. Package removal
does not remove this directory.
.TP
.I ~/.config/whitecube/cube-chrootables.conf
Preferences shared intentionally by Studio and the bundled Whitecube edition.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sudo (8),
.BR debootstrap (8)
